  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Preheat oven to 200°C/180°C fan-forced.\n• Finely chop garlic.\n• In a medium saucepan, melt butter with a dash of olive oil over medium heat. Add ½ the garlic and cook until fragrant, 1-2 minutes.\n• Add basmati rice, water (for the rice) and a generous pinch of salt, stir, then bring to the boil.\n• Reduce heat to low and cover with a lid. Cook for 10 minutes, then remove from heat and keep covered until rice is tender and water is absorbed, 10 minutes. TIP: The rice will finish cooking in its own steam, so don't peek!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/63731802119b77e3270fde68/step-29b12594.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• While rice is cooking, slice mini flourtortillas into quarters. Finely chop brown onion. Finely chop cucumber. Roughly chop coriander and pickled jalapenos (if using). Drain and rinse sweetcorn (see ingredients) and black beans.\n• Divide mini flourtortillas between two lined oven trays (don’t worry if they overlap). Drizzle with olive oil and season with salt. Bake until lightly golden and crispy, 8-10 minutes.\n• Meanwhile, heat a large frying pan over high heat. Add corn kernels and cook until lightly browned, 4-5 minutes. Transfer to a medium bowl.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/63731802119b77e3270fde68/step-adb22940.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Return frying pan to medium-high heat with a drizzle of olive oil.\n• SPICY! The spice blend is hot, use less if you're sensitive to heat. Add onion and cook until tender, 3-4 minutes. Add remaining garlic, Tex-Mex spice blend, tomato paste and cook until fragrant, 1 minute.\n• Add black beans and water (for the beans), and cook until slightly thickened, 2-3 minutes.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/63731802119b77e3270fde68/step-475f9ca1.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• While beans are simmering, combine the corn, cucumber, coriander, a drizzle of white wine vinegar and olive oil. Season to taste.\n• Divide garlic rice, Tex-Mex black beans and charred corn salsa between bowls.\n• Top with light sour cream, pickled jalapenos and tortilla chips to serve. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/63731802119b77e3270fde68/step-830f6024.jpg"
    }
  ]
